{"v":1,"seq":469,"ts":"2026-11-25T19:03:54.893Z","job":"bumper-kart-football-3-20261125-1","type":"note","package":"core","round":12,"text":"- `possession_median_f` is 30, outside 240–600. The player answered that the ball stays fully loose and the 4-second possession target is dropped.\n- Sparks and the metal clang now play on every hard kart contact (`flank`, `rear`, `nose`, `clash`, `whirl_block`, `ram_*`), not sparks on rams only. This follows the change request. Shake is still rams involving p1 and goals only.\n- Values changed this round: `react.knock_m` 1.15 to 1.5. New values: `react.spin_whip` 0.9, `hit_fx.bang_db` 0, and `hit_fx.spark_scale` (0.9 to 1.8 by contact kind).\n- The extra separation is on the visuals only. Kart velocities, hit-stop frames and the contact table are unchanged.\n- Camera differs from the contract (change request 1): back 15, up 14, fov 54 instead of 8, 7, 46. Pitch is set between the kart and the far goal, it follows sideways only partly, stops short of the near end, and leans in briefly on big hits involving p1. Its heading never turns.\n- Goals are 14 m wide and 2.5 m tall (not 4 m), with team-coloured frame, net and floor goal line. The boards are drawn 1.3 m high (not 1 m).\n- After a goal, the kickoff ball sits 5 m off centre (`match.kickoff_lean_m`) instead of centred.\n- A spun kart's visual makes up to 4 turns, easing out (`react.spin_turns`).\n\nInvariants (V3) has now finished and **passed**: runs are deterministic, with no errors, and frame time and entity counts are within budget. This replaces the \"still running\" row in my table.\n\nThe one expected failure is still median possession, 30 frames against a bound of 240–600. You chose to drop that target, so the Foreman needs to remove the bound. The files and deviations listed above are unchanged."}
